 ## Background
-Grid Embedding is described in VC-SDFGen, an unofficial repository [S1, unofficial]. It is used to store and optimize shape-specific latent codes for 3D models. The Trainable 3D Saliency Grid variant originates from HollowNeRF, which proposes pruning hashgrid-based NeRFs by learning sparsity patterns to reclaim capacity spent on internal occluded regions [S2].
